### Statements that don't rise

The contrast is [andrich_mudfold](https://itemresponsewarehouse.org/tables/andrich_mudfold/): 54 graduate students in an introductory measurement course, each agreeing (1) or disagreeing (0) with eight statements about capital punishment ([Andrich, 1988](https://doi.org/10.1177/014662168801200105)). Its job is to show items whose curves don't rise with the score. The statements span opinion from strongly against to strongly in favour; we put them in Andrich's order. With 54 respondents every proportion below is noisy.


::: {.cell}

